        //
        // Unless... I make the env accessor return HOME for path resolution
        // but the actual file at the resolved path has keys. But Read(env)
        // does its own path resolution with the same env, gets the same path,
        // finds the file, reads keys. present.Count > 0.
        //
        // I'm going in circles. Let me just test the realistic code paths
        // that CAN happen:
        //
        // Path A: no HOME set → Read throws InvalidOperationException → empty
        //         → present empty → guard: ResolvePathForCurrentUser also throws
        //         → caught → "zero keys — using static config"
        //
        // Path B: HOME set, file doesn't exist → Read returns empty
        //         → present empty → guard: ResolvePathForCurrentUser succeeds
